# Raw run output (requests/, samples/, logs/, raw.json, report.md per run) is
# not tracked. The curated RECORDS are, and they must be visible to
# `git status` rather than needing `git add -f`: the 2026-08-15 instance-store
# wipe destroyed the evidence for six sections of the published report because
# everything under here was ignored wholesale.
#
# `results/` alone cannot be negated inside: git does not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so a `!results/.../x.json` after it never matches. The
# `results/**` + `!results/**/` pair keeps the directories walkable so the file
# negations below can take effect.
results/**
!results/**/
!results/**/analysis.json
!results/**/run.json
!results/**/hostcdp.jsonl
!results/**/summary.json
!results/**/meta.json
!results/**/charts/
!results/**/charts/*.svg
!results/**/summary.md
# DNS-campaign evidence: the in-clone resolver check (plus the per-bracket
# copies verify-dns-pre/before-run/after-run.json that dns-evidence.json lists
# in verify_files), the campaign verdict, the diagnostic summary, the
# resolver-owner log and the campaign index.
!results/**/verify-dns.json
!results/**/verify-dns-*.json
!results/**/dns-evidence.json
!results/**/diag/summary.json
!results/**/dns-owner.log
# The replay server's own logs and the campaign's per-bracket record of what
# it served: dns-evidence.json records the sha256 of all three and
# campaign_summary refuses the run unless every one is present and matches.
!results/**/corpus-dns.log
!results/**/corpus-access.log
!results/**/replay-queries.log
!results/**/campaign-*-summary.json
# The withdrawal marker: its first line is why the run may never be quoted,
# and campaign_summary refuses the run while it is present.
!results/**/WITHDRAWN
# The corpus-extra campaign (memory and per-render CPU, fcvm clones against host
# containers): the analysis, the records it is recomputable from, and the bytes
# that produced them. Its raw logs are deliberately absent -- see the commit that
# added the run for what stayed on the box and why.
!results/**/provenance.json
!results/**/comparison.json
!results/**/cputime.json
!results/**/samples.jsonl
!results/**/phase.log
!results/**/corpus-serve.status
!results/**/memory-cpu-analysis.md
!results/**/recompute_memory_cpu.py
# reqbench.jsonl is analysis.json's only input: analysis_identity.inputs pins it
# by sha256 and every headline cites line ranges in it, so without it a published
# number survives but stops being recomputable.
!results/**/reqbench.jsonl
# The scripts a run froze beside itself. provenance.json hashes them; this is the
# copy those hashes name, and for a script that is not in the tree it is the only
# record of what ran.
!results/**/harness/*
# A gate that fired: the diag summary of a campaign that was refused, kept so the
# refusal is checkable rather than only remembered.
!results/**/notes/*.json
!results/**/cpuprobe-*-curated.json
!results/**/webkit-host-probe.json
__pycache__/
